load @term/seed/code/axiom
  find axiom

# An axiom schema: not a single axiom but a template standing for infinitely many, one for each way of filling its
# blanks. Separation and replacement in set theory, and induction in arithmetic, are schemas: induction is one axiom per
# predicate. A schema is how a first-order theory expresses a second-order idea within its means. The form carries the
# template axiom; the instances are its fillings.
form axiom-schema
  link template, like axiom
